snip">Anne Frank was a German-born Jewish girl whose family fled to Amsterdam and, from 1942, hid from the Nazi occupiers in a secret annex behind her father's business.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/anne-hutchinson"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/anne-hutchinson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Anne Hutchinson</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Anne Hutchinson was an English-born Puritan spiritual adviser in the Massachusetts Bay Colony.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/anne-marie-louise-dorleans-duchess-of-montpensier"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/anne-marie-louise-dorleans-duchess-of-montpensier.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Anne Marie Louise d'Orléans, Duchess of Montpensier</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Anne Marie Louise d'Orléans, known as La Grande Mademoiselle, was a cousin of Louis XIV and the richest heiress in France.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/anne-of-brittany"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/anne-of-brittany.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Anne of Brittany</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Anne of Brittany was duchess of Brittany from 1488 and twice queen of France, through marriage to Charles VIII in 1491 and Louis XII in 1499.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/anne-of-cleves"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/anne-of-cleves.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Anne of Cleves</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Anne of Cleves was a daughter of Duke John III of Cleves and the fourth wife of Henry VIII of England.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href