dth="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Antiochus VII Sidetes</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Antiochus VII Sidetes was a Seleucid king who attempted to restore the dynasty's power in the second century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-xiii-asiaticus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/antiochus-xiii-asiaticus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Antiochus XIII Asiaticus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Antiochus XIII Asiaticus was the last king of the Seleucid dynasty, son of Antiochus X and Cleopatra Selene.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/antioquia-department"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/antioquia-department.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Antioquia Department</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Antioquia is a department of north-western Colombia in the Central and Western Cordilleras; its capital is Medellín.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/antipater"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/antipater.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Antipater</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Antipater was a Macedonian general and statesman who served Philip II and governed Macedon and Greece while Alexander the Great campaigned in Asia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/antipope-anacletus-ii"><span class="enc-name">Antipope Anacletus II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Anacletus II, born Pietro Pierleoni, was an antipope from 1130 to 1138.</span></a></li></ul>
